    "legend": "Arterioles within and occasionally outside a metanephric stromal tumour frequently demonstrate angiodysplasia. The majority of this arterial wall is markedly thickened, having undergone myxoid degeneration. The normally spindled smooth muscle cells have become epithelioid. These vessels can rupture, leading to haemorrhage.",
